From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: odroid-go-ultra: power off the RK817 by its SLEEP pin

The driver set DEV_OFF on the RK817 and then on the RK818. Powered off
that way, the RK817 only comes back on with the power key, and not
reliably when USB power is present: the RK818 then powers up on its own
(ON_SOURCE plug-in), the RK817 that feeds the boot CPU stays off, and the
SoC hangs half powered (a few garbage bytes on the UART) until the
battery is cut by holding the power key with USB unplugged.

Do what the vendor kernel does (Hardkernel odroidgoU-4.9.y,
rk817_shutdown_prepare() and rk818_shutdown()): set the RK817 SLEEP pin
function to "power down", active high, and DEV_OFF on the RK818 only.
The SoC holds the SLEEP pin low while it runs; when the RK818 cuts its
power the pin goes high and the RK817 powers down, and it comes back on
with the RK818. Tested: power off, plug USB in, the board wakes up and
boots cleanly (ON_SOURCE plug-in), as with the factory system.

--- a/drivers/power/reset/odroid-go-ultra-poweroff.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/odroid-go-ultra-poweroff.c
@@ -17,7 +17,21 @@
  * - RK818 (manages the battery and USB-C power supply)
  * - RK817
  * Both PMICs feeds power to the S922X SoC, so they must be powered-off in sequence.
- * Vendor does power-off the RK817 first, then the RK818 so here we follow this sequence.
+ *
+ * The vendor kernel (Hardkernel odroidgoU-4.9.y, rk817_shutdown_prepare() and
+ * rk818_shutdown()) sets DEV_OFF on the RK818 only. Before that the RK817
+ * SLEEP pin is set to the "power down" function, active high: the pin is low
+ * while the SoC runs and goes high once the RK818 has cut the SoC's power,
+ * which then powers the RK817 down. Turned off this way, the RK817 comes back
+ * on by itself whenever the RK818 does (power key or USB plug-in).
+ *
+ * Setting DEV_OFF on the RK817 instead leaves it waiting for the power key
+ * alone: with USB power present the RK818 then comes up without it, and the
+ * SoC is left half powered and dead until the battery is disconnected or the
+ * power key is held down long enough with USB unplugged.
+ *
+ * The polarity is set together with the function: changing the polarity of a
+ * pin that is already in its active state would trigger the function at once.
  */
 
 struct odroid_go_ultra_poweroff_data {
@@ -48,10 +62,12 @@
 
 	dev_info(poweroff_data->dev, "Setting PMICs for power off");
 
-	/* RK817 */
-	ret = regmap_update_bits(rk817, RK817_SYS_CFG(3), DEV_OFF, DEV_OFF);
+	/* RK817: power down on its SLEEP pin going high */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(rk817, RK817_SYS_CFG(3),
+				 RK817_SLPPIN_FUNC_MSK | RK817_SLPPOL_MSK,
+				 SLPPIN_DN_FUN | RK817_SLPPOL_H);
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(poweroff_data->dev, "failed to poweroff rk817\n");
+		dev_err(poweroff_data->dev, "failed to set the rk817 sleep pin\n");
 		return notifier_from_errno(ret);
 	}
 
